---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import InquiryForm from '../components/InquiryForm.astro';
import ServiceArtwork from '../components/ServiceArtwork.astro';
import '../styles/services.css';
import '../styles/services-page.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Business Services | Cloud & Capital" description="Technology cost reviews, AI and workflow reviews, and practical setup for service businesses. Clear findings, a defined scope, and a useful next step with Diana Molski.">
  <main id="main-content" class="offer-page business-services">
    <section class="services-shell services-hero" aria-labelledby="services-title">
      <div class="services-hero-copy">
        <p class="service-kicker">Business services · Cloud &amp; Capital</p>
        <h1 id="services-title">Your tools should<br /><em>earn their keep.</em></h1>
        <p class="services-lede">Technology cost reviews, AI &amp; workflow reviews, and practical setup for service businesses.</p>
        <p class="services-aside">Because another subscription isn’t always the answer.</p>
        <div class="services-actions"><a class="offer-button" href="#offers">Explore the services <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="service-text-link" href="#inquiry">Ask me about your business →</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="services-hero-art"><ServiceArtwork kind="hero" /><p>Make sense of it. Then make it useful.</p></div>
    </section>
    <nav class="services-shell service-jump-links" aria-label="Choose a service"><span>What needs a second look?</span><a href="#technology-cost-review">Technology Cost Review →</a><a href="#workflow-review">AI &amp; Workflow Review →</a><a href="#practical-setup">Practical Setup →</a></nav>
    <section id="offers" class="services-shell offers-section" aria-labelledby="offers-title">
      <div class="services-section-heading"><div><p class="service-kicker">Three ways to work together</p><h2 id="offers-title">A useful place to start.</h2></div><p>For owners and operations leads at agencies, consultancies, and other service businesses. Bring a bill, a recurring task, or a clearly defined project.</p></div>
      <div class="service-cards">
        <article id="technology-cost-review" class="service-card cost-card">
          <div class="service-card-art"><ServiceArtwork kind="cost" /></div>
          <div class="service-card-content"><p class="service-kicker">01 · Understand the spending</p><h3>Technology Cost Review</h3><p class="service-question">“Is this worth what we’re paying?”</p><p>For confusing software bills, overlapping subscriptions, and upcoming renewals.</p><div class="service-deliverables"><h4>You’ll leave with</h4><ul><li>A clear spending breakdown</li><li>Keep, review, or change options</li><li>A prioritized next-step list</li></ul></div><details class="service-scope"><summary>Scope &amp; example</summary><p>One business, up to 10 software or AI subscriptions, and three recent billing months plus annual charges and renewal terms. Findings account for use, dependencies, and the effort of changing tools.</p><p>Cancellations and migrations are separate. Detailed cloud allocation, commitments, or architecture need their own FinOps scope.</p><a href="/services/examples#cost">See a fictional cost review →</a></details><a class="service-card-cta" href="#inquiry">Ask about a cost review <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        </article>
        <article id="workflow-review" class="service-card workflow-card">
          <div class="service-card-art"><ServiceArtwork kind="workflow" /></div>
          <div class="service-card-content"><p class="service-kicker">02 · Understand the work</p><h3>AI &amp; Workflow Review</h3><p class="service-question">“Why does this take so long?”</p><p>For reports and recurring tasks with too much copying, checking, or chasing.</p><div class="service-deliverables"><h4>You’ll leave with</h4><ul><li>A map of where work gets stuck</li><li>Options using existing tools, automation, or AI</li><li>One practical pilot plan</li></ul></div><details class="service-scope"><summary>Scope &amp; example</summary><p>One workflow across up to three tools, using two or three redacted examples. We compare simpler processes, existing features, automation, and AI—including costs, checking, and maintenance.</p><p>Your pilot plan includes a success measure and an owner. You can use it independently; building it is separately scoped.</p><a href="/services/examples#workflow">See a fictional workflow review →</a></details><a class="service-card-cta" href="#inquiry">Ask about a workflow review <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        </article>
        <article id="practical-setup" class="service-card setup-card">
          <div class="service-card-art"><ServiceArtwork kind="setup" /></div>
          <div class="service-card-content"><p class="service-kicker">03 · Put the change to work</p><h3>Practical Setup</h3><p class="service-question">“Can you help me build it?”</p><p>For a reporting template, intake process, or small automation with a clear goal.</p><div class="service-deliverables"><h4>You’ll leave with</h4><ul><li>The agreed setup, ready to use</li><li>Checks for normal use and exceptions</li><li>Instructions and a proper handoff</li></ul></div><details class="service-scope"><summary>Scope &amp; approach</summary><p>One agreed result across up to three compatible tools, individually quoted. We agree the inputs, deliverable, tests, and maintenance owner before work starts.</p><p>A paid review isn’t required when the project is clear. New features and ongoing support are agreed separately.</p></details><a class="service-card-cta" href="#inquiry">Ask about a setup <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="service-choice-note">A bill <em>and</em> a workflow? Or not sure where to start? <a href="#inquiry">Tell me what’s happening.</a> We’ll find the right starting point before paid work.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="services-method" aria-labelledby="process-title"><div class="services-shell"><div class="services-section-heading"><div><p class="service-kicker">A clear scope, from the start</p><h2 id="process-title">Here’s how we work.</h2></div><p>Start in writing. Use a call or recorded walkthrough when it helps.</p></div><ol class="method-steps"><li><span class="method-number">01</span><h3>Tell me what’s stuck.</h3><p>The question, the tools, and what you’d like to change.</p></li><li><span class="method-number">02</span><h3>Agree the work.</h3><p>A defined scope, fixed quote, timeline, and handoff before we begin.</p></li><li><span class="method-number">03</span><h3>Get something useful.</h3><p>Clear findings or the agreed setup, with a practical next step.</p></li></ol></div></section>
    <section class="services-shell services-about" aria-labelledby="reviewer-title"><div class="services-portrait"><img src="/images/diana-molski-portrait.png" alt="Diana Molski, founder of Cloud & Capital" width="820" height="806" loading="lazy" /><p>Diana Molski · Los Angeles</p></div><div><p class="service-kicker">Your reviewer &amp; builder</p><h2 id="reviewer-title">Hi, I’m Diana.<br /><em>I like a good money question.</em></h2><p>A finance degree, a background in wealth management at Morgan Stanley, and a habit of asking what the numbers actually support.</p><p>Today I bring that perspective to technology spending, recurring reporting, and practical tools for business owners.</p><div class="services-credentials"><span>FinOps Practitioner &amp; FOCUS Analyst</span><span>AWS Cloud Practitioner</span><span>Azure AI Fundamentals</span></div><a class="service-text-link" href="/#about">More about my background →</a></div></section>
    <section class="services-proof" aria-labelledby="proof-title"><div class="services-shell proof-grid"><div><p class="service-kicker">Built by Cloud &amp; Capital</p><h2 id="proof-title">I build tools that make<br /><em>the numbers easier to use.</em></h2><p>AI Cost Lens compares the cost behind a usable AI result. Cloud Cost Guard brings cloud, AI, and software spending into view.</p><a class="service-text-link" href="/tools">Explore the tools →</a></div><figure><a href="https://lens.cloudandcapital.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Explore AI Cost Lens"><img src="/images/ai-cost-lens-cost-anatomy-wide.png" alt="AI Cost Lens screen comparing model, infrastructure, and human review costs" width="2048" height="901" loading="lazy" /></a><figcaption>AI Cost Lens · Illustrative tool example, not a client result.</figcaption></figure></div></section>
    <section class="services-shell services-extras" aria-label="Resources and education"><a class="resource-feature" href="/resources/software-renewal"><div class="resource-mark" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 90 110"><path d="M20 14h49v78H20z"/><path d="m28 36 4 4 8-9m-12 24 4 4 8-9m-12 24 4 4 8-9M47 35h13M47 54h13M47 73h13"/></svg></div><div><p class="service-kicker">A little help before you hire</p><h3>Before you renew that software.</h3><p>Eight questions for your next keep-or-change decision.</p><span class="service-text-link">Use the free checklist →</span></div></a><div class="learning-feature"><p class="service-kicker">Here for the markets?</p><h3>Let’s make those<br /><em>make sense, too.</em></h3><p>Investing and trading education has its own place.</p><a class="service-text-link" href="/learn">Explore investing &amp; trading lessons →</a></div></section>
    <section class="services-shell services-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div><p class="service-kicker">Before we start</p><h2 id="faq-title">A few practical<br /><em>questions.</em></h2></div><div><details><summary>What will it cost?</summary><p>You receive a defined scope and fixed quote before work begins. Setup fees depend on the result and systems involved.</p></details><details><summary>Do I have to buy new software?</summary><p>Existing tools and simpler processes are considered first. Any proposed external cost is made explicit.</p></details><details><summary>Is a review a commitment to a bigger project?</summary><p>No. A review delivers findings and a next step you can use independently. Implementation is separately scoped when useful.</p></details><details><summary>Are savings guaranteed?</summary><p>Findings explain evidence and assumptions. Time freed up is kept separate from cash savings; the recommendation may be to keep your existing system.</p></details></div></section>
    <section id="inquiry" class="services-contact" aria-labelledby="inquiry-title"><div class="services-shell services-contact-grid"><div><p class="service-kicker">Let’s start with your question</p><h2 id="inquiry-title">What’s getting<br /><em>stuck?</em></h2><p>A few lines are enough. You don’t need to choose a service first.</p><p>I’ll reply with any questions, then a scope and quote if there’s a useful project.</p><p class="contact-privacy">Leave out financial records, passwords, and sensitive client information.</p></div><InquiryForm kind="business" /></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
